- Implemented revision: `b45bf5df`
- Pinned Java source: `rocketmq-all-5.5.1` tag, `2ed890cd27b047cc124638aa3c80e391dde942b8`
- Scope: retry-topic publication through `MQClientInstance`'s internal `DefaultMQProducer`

## Finding and change

Pinned Java `MQClientInstance` constructs `DefaultMQProducer` with group
`CLIENT_INNER_PRODUCER` and starts its implementation with the client factory.
The producer defaults are `sendMsgTimeout=3000`,
`retryTimesWhenSendFailed=2`, and
`retryAnotherBrokerWhenNotStoreOK=false`. Its default retry-response codes are
`TOPIC_NOT_EXIST`, `SERVICE_NOT_AVAILABLE`, `SYSTEM_ERROR`, `SYSTEM_BUSY`,
`NO_PERMISSION`, `NO_BUYER_ID`, `NOT_IN_CURRENT_UNIT`, and `GO_AWAY`.
`sendDefaultImpl` spends the send timeout across route lookup and up to three
synchronous sends, avoids the previous Broker when another route is available,
retries transport/client failures and only the listed Broker responses.

Rust retry-topic fallback now uses this default timeout, attempt count, previous
Broker avoidance, and response-code retry rule. The behavior covered here is
the default `sendLatencyEnable=false` selector; Java's optional latency-fault
selector when that setting is enabled remains part of the broader P18-V01
audit.

